=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play firewall/edit-2230 --------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the Firewall screen proposed for slice 4,$
# drawn from what real code reads of a simulated host$
# (firewall.Incoming.Check, ufw.Read, pve.ReadFirewall,$
# sshd.ReadEffective, reload.ReadBound), Enable the real$
# steps.PlanUFWEnable on the real plan/apply engine. Install,$
# Disable, the runlevel and the profiles' plans are the$
# gallery's stand-ins, unit (b)'s to build. Nothing on this$
# machine changes: every command and file is the fake's, and its$
# record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: firewall/edit-2230$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. Port 2230 in hardn's drop-$
# in, sshd not reloaded, so still on 22, ufw inactive. What$
# accepts SSH is not what is configured, so Enable refuses$
# (decision 2; mock stale-listener has what the real plan does).$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [ ] Firewall             Not Configured inactive$
$
# ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [ ] Status               Inactive$
   -  Incoming policy      Deny$
  [ ] At boot              No$
$
# SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] [::]:2230            Not filtered Not bound$
  [ ] 0.0.0.0:2230         Not filtered Not bound$
  [ ] [::]:22              Not filtered Not configured$
  [ ] 0.0.0.0:22           Not filtered Not configured$
$
# Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  No firewall rules configured$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable firewall      Let SSH through, then start ufw$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 1$
$
# Warning$
# sshd isn't listening where its config says, so hardn can't$
# tell which ports SSH uses. Reload sshd or restart ssh.socket,$
# then try again.$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [ ] Firewall             Not Configured inactive$
$
# ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [ ] Status               Inactive$
   -  Incoming policy      Deny$
  [ ] At boot              No$
$
# SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] [::]:2230            Not filtered Not bound$
  [ ] 0.0.0.0:2230         Not filtered Not bound$
  [ ] [::]:22              Not filtered Not configured$
  [ ] 0.0.0.0:22           Not filtered Not configured$
$
# Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  No firewall rules configured$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable firewall      Let SSH through, then start ufw$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

